hey what's up youtube hope you're having  a great day so i wanted to take a short  amount of time to talk about elden ring  and sort of the backlash the game is  getting from certain gamers and  streamers who are having a tough time  progressing and feel discouraged to play  the game at all i completely understand  how you feel because i remember when i  first started playing souls games myself  i actually started with dark souls 3 and  really struggled with it initially until  i started to understand more about how  the game worked i got absolutely  destroyed by the first boss gundyr  dozens of times before i finally beat  him and i can tell you i wasn't happy  after i beat him i was a bit discouraged  but over time i started to learn more  things about the game that made my time  playing it easier and increased my  enjoyment of the game immensely so much  so that i can say that the souls games  meaning dark souls 1 through 3  bloodborne and skiro are some of my  favorite games of all time even though i  didn't play the games in order of when  they first launched so the big issue  i've been seeing is that the first main  boss you're going to come across market  is too difficult the advanced move and  range of damage that margate can do  against you as a player is hard however  i believe that margate is intentionally  difficult in hopes that players will go  and discover other areas and eventually  come back to market when they're  stronger because that's the beauty of  elden ring you don't have to follow the  path all the way up to the castle to  fight margaret you can go anywhere your  heart and sense of discovery desires for  some people this may be sort of  overwhelming because of what they're  used to when it comes to playing a video  game most video games tell you exactly  where to go and tell you exactly what to  do eldon ring will not hold your hand  and that is meant to be a good thing the  developers know that you the player are  smart enough and capable enough to deal  with the challenges that the game gives  you and this is still pretty different  from the usual souls game experience  which has you make your way through a  generally linear level until you come  across a boss and the only way to  progress through the rest of the game is  for you to beat that boss so you'll just  fight the boss over and over again until  you beat it and then you can progress in  eldon ring you can absolutely do that  you can bash your head into the wall  fighting the boss again and again and  you will eventually beat it and you will  probably walk out of that fight more  frustrated than happy which is not the  experience the developers want you to  have they understand that past souls  games were really uninviting to most  gamers since there is no difficulty  setting there is no easy mode even in  elden ring everyone who plays the game  is going up against the same challenges  as you in the exact same ways but it's  up to you as the player to decide how  you want to handle those challenges in  your own special way  depending on your class your weapon the  skill arts that you use the spells that  you can obtain almost anything and that  has been the case with all the past  games as well but the developers this  time around with elden ring made it more  accessible than ever to feel progression  within the game you do not have to  follow the path put in front of you  because they do put a path in front of  you literally and on your map to walk  all the way up to the castle and fight  margaret right off the rip but you do  not have to follow this path there is no  linear pathway to progression you can go  in any direction you want and nothing is  going to stop you and this is a far  stretch from the usual formula of  bashing your head against a wall until  you finally overcome the challenge they  still give you that option like i said  and if you're into that sort of thing  but the decisions you can make on how to  handle the challenges 